18 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178714 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186178719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178714 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178714 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178714 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "409e6aaa-e12a-5788-b4cb-0ef67baf6ca1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178715 #edb/ref 1080 "22.4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178715 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178715 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8f98eba5-3905-554d-9a31-d6d0645340bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178716 #edb/ref 1080 "-22.4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178716 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178716 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "feebfb06-6943-5ff2-921b-ddc0bef864dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178717 #edb/ref 1080 "20.2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178717 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178717 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1091d78c-6247-5b85-bdc5-bc04d318f86f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178718 #edb/ref 1080 "-20.4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178718 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178718 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "38c6376d-3646-590a-928e-9aa66371b7b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178719 #edb/ref 1080 "20.4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178719 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186178719 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "66c47c60-a2ae-5faf-afaa-62aec47769f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179450 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12963" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179450 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $(-9) \\cdot (-5)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179450 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66ce7121-0e0c-5108-86c4-3c11f4434b5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179450 #edb/ref 1074 "We have a product of two negative numbers, $\\color{red}-9$ and ${\\color{red}-5}$. So the product will be positive:\n$45$\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $9$ and $5$ without any signs:\n\n$$\n9 \\cdot 5 = 45\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-9)} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-5)} = {\\color{blue}45}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179451 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12965" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179451 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $(-3) \\cdot (-5) \\cdot (-10)$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179451 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ce77ea1c-ff60-5548-abdf-d64e23574943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179451 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of two negatives, which gives a positive:\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-3)} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-5)} = {\\color{blue}15}\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{\\color{red}(-3)} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-5)}}_{\\large {\\color{blue}15}} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-10)} = {\\color{blue}15} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-10)}\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that a positive times a negative gives a negative:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}15} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-10)} = {\\color{red}-(15\\cdot 10)} = {\\color{red}-150}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179452 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12966" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179452 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\left(-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{10}{3}\\right)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179452 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "741da5ab-8c69-5eff-af12-3fbadc2d9fb4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179452 #edb/ref 1074 "We have a product of two negative numbers, so the product will be positive, and we can drop the minus signs as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\cdot (-\\frac{10}{3}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{10}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{10}{3} &= \\frac{1 \\cdot 10}{2 \\cdot 3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5 \\cdot 2}{2 \\cdot 3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5 \\cdot 2}{2 \\cdot 3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179453 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12968" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179453 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $(-3.4) \\cdot 3.8$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179453 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "375a9118-9e3c-5fda-b787-5f3012296150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179453 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the product of a negative number and a positive number, which gives a negative number.\n\n$$\n(-3.4) \\cdot 3.8 = -(3.4 \\cdot 3.8) = -12.92\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179821 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179821 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179821 #edb/ref 1039 "Multiplying Two Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179821 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179821 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "8332e831-fb93-567f-ae21-a80716a57f70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179822 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179822 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179822 #edb/ref 1039 "Multiplying More Than Two Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179822 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179822 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "33b32ea7-dd7d-5e41-8fdb-142ec9da82c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179823 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179823 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179823 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179823 #edb/ref 1039 "Multiplying Fractions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179823 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179823 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "192eeaef-4283-5db1-9a8f-0f2fbff163d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179824 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049194 #edb/ref 17592